# The offline path -- tests, red-team corpus, quality gate, demo --
# needs NONE of these. Everything below is only needed to wire up a
# real speech-to-text or text-to-speech provider.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in only what you need. Never commit .env.

# Speech-to-text. The provider implementation in src/audio.py accepts
# an already-configured client, so the SDK is only imported if you
# construct that client yourself.
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=

# Text-to-speech.
# GTTS_LANG=en

# Where the call recording is written. One file per call, appended in
# order, never overwritten mid-call.
# CALL_RECORDING_PATH=demo.wav

# The published non-emergency line. Used in the fallback message the
# agent gives a caller it cannot understand. This prototype does not
# dial it. Fill in the real published number for your city before
# deploying; leave it blank here so no real public-service number is
# committed to a public repository.
# PUBLIC_NON_EMERGENCY_LINE=
